{"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"Hypergraphs"}],"title":"Hypergraphs","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","externalID":"Hypergraphs"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/DirectedIncidenceGraphView","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceList","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Extended Modules","anchor":"Extended-Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/GraphProtocols"]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs","type":"topic","title":"Hypergraphs","abstract":[]},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/UndirectedIncidenceList":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/undirectedincidencelist","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph stored as an incidence list: a row per hyperedge of its members and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row per vertex of its memberships. The undirected counterpart of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":", named as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedAdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":" is. ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", the bit-matrix representation, is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"undirected one of its pair, because “oriented incidence matrix” is the established name of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other.)"}],"title":"UndirectedIncidenceList","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndirectedIncidenceList","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndirectedIncidenceList","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/GraphProtocols":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/graphprotocols"},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/IncidenceList":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencelist","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceList","title":"IncidenceList","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed hypergraph stored as an incidence list: each hyperedge’s sources and targets, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each vertex’s out- and in-hyperedges (Gallo’s forward and backward stars), as two planes of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":"’s storage. Unprefixed, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":" is the directed one of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pair. ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" is the matrix form; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" is undirected, because"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“oriented incidence matrix” is the established name.)"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidenceList","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceList","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/DirectedIncidenceGraphView":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/DirectedIncidenceGraphView","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/directedincidencegraphview","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"type":"text","text":" whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" and whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" is hyperedge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", with an arc "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i → n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" for each source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p → j"},{"type":"text","text":" for each target "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"j"},{"type":"text","text":". A vertex on both sides of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the 2-cycle"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i → n + p → i"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/IncidenceGraphView":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"IncidenceGraphView","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"type":"text","text":" whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" and whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is hyperedge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", with an edge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{i, n + p}"},{"type":"text","text":" for each incidence. It is bipartite and simple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(vertices on the left, hyperedges on the right), an empty hyperedge is an isolated vertex, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it loses nothing."}]}}}